# terminfo source for felis — TERM=xterm-felis
#
# Install:   tic -x -o ~/.terminfo share/terminfo/felis.terminfo
# Verify:    infocmp -x xterm-felis
#
# This entry is `use=xterm-256color` plus ONLY the capabilities felis
# was verified to implement (see docs/reference/terminal-identity.md). It
# deliberately omits the
# DCS-form `Sync` capability: felis implements synchronized output via
# the DECSET form (CSI ? 2026 h/l) only, so advertising the DCS form
# would make tmux drive an unimplemented path. Likewise it does not
# fabricate kitty-namespaced state — felis answers protocol queries
# truthfully instead.
#
# Capability provenance (felis-vt / felis-grid, audited 2026-05-29):
#   Tc / setrgbf / setrgbb  — truecolor, colon-form RGB sub-parameters
#   Smulx / Setulc          — styled underlines + underline color
#   smxx / rmxx             — strikethrough (SGR 9 / 29)
#   BE / BD                 — bracketed paste (?2004)
#   XF / fe / fd / kxIN/kxOUT — focus events (?1004)
#   Ss / Se                 — DECSCUSR cursor shapes
#   Cs / Cr                 — set / reset cursor color (OSC 12 / 112)
#   fullkbd                 — Kitty keyboard protocol
#
# The cancellations below drop xterm-256color inheritances felis does
# not implement: SCS is parsed but no-op (REQ-211), so acsc / smacs /
# rmacs — and `sgr`, whose %p9 arm switches into it — would make
# ncurses draw boxes as literal `qqlk`; and `xr` / `rv` claim xterm's
# XTVERSION and DA2 version replies, which felis answers as itself.
#
# `pairs#0x7fff` is not cosmetic: a number above 32767 makes ncurses
# 6.1+ tic emit the 32-bit binary format (magic 0o1036), which the
# ncurses 6.0 shipped in macOS cannot read at all — every system
# tput / vim / less inside felis then reports an unknown terminal.
# That same reader caps an entry at 4096 bytes, which the compiled
# entry must stay under (the Nix build asserts both).

xterm-felis|felis terminal emulator,
	Tc,
	acsc@,
	pairs#0x7fff,
	rmacs@,
	rv@,
	sgr@,
	smacs@,
	xr@,
	XF,
	fullkbd,
	BD=\E[?2004l,
	BE=\E[?2004h,
	Cr=\E]112\007,
	Cs=\E]12;%p1%s\007,
	Se=\E[2 q,
	Setulc=\E[58\:2\:%p1%{65536}%/%d\:%p1%{256}%/%{255}%&%d\:%p1%{255}%&%dm,
	Smulx=\E[4\:%p1%dm,
	Ss=\E[%p1%d q,
	fd=\E[?1004l,
	fe=\E[?1004h,
	kxIN=\E[I,
	kxOUT=\E[O,
	rmxx=\E[29m,
	setrgbb=\E[48\:2\:%p1%d\:%p2%d\:%p3%dm,
	setrgbf=\E[38\:2\:%p1%d\:%p2%d\:%p3%dm,
	smxx=\E[9m,
	use=xterm-256color,
